{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7878","id":5216783855,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNvHN7w","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7878","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7878.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7878.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7878","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7878/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7878/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7878/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/ed0825d33f597801985c96c282ea770408373cc0","number":7878,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(id): bound aggregate pending email-code state (#5749)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #5749.\n\n## What\n\n`DirectoryAuth.issue_code` kept every unexpired pending email code with no size bound: repeated requests for unique addresses grew the pending-code map (and the O(pending) expiry sweep on each issuance) without limit.\n\nThis adds two hard caps in `pkgs/id/src/directory_auth.rs`:\n\n- `CODE_PENDING_LIMIT = 4096` — global pending codes across all addresses, so the map and issuance cost stay bounded (O(cap)).\n- `CODE_PENDING_PER_ACCOUNT = 16` — per-account pending codes, so one account cannot consume the global capacity and starve unrelated accounts.\n\nSemantics preserved / chosen:\n\n- Expired entries are swept before the caps are checked — expiry always frees capacity.\n- A new address that would pass a cap is refused deterministically with `Refusal::RateLimited`; no unrelated valid code is evicted to make room.\n- Replacing the code for an address already in the map (resend past the existing 60s cooldown) is not new state and always works at capacity.\n- Verification, one-time use, and the 5-attempt limit are unchanged.\n- `SignInEmail` already ignores issuance failures, so its externally visible response stays uniform whether a code was issued or refused; `AddEmail` propagates the refusal to the signed-in caller on purpose.\n\n## Tests\n\n`cargo test directory_auth` in pkgs/id (laptop): 15 passed, 0 failed, including three new tests:\n\n- `pending_codes_are_capped_globally_and_refusal_is_deterministic` — fills all 4096 slots, refusal is deterministic, nothing evicted, resend-at-capacity replaces, replaced code verifies exactly once.\n- `one_account_cannot_consume_the_whole_pending_capacity` — per-account cap binds at 16 while another account still issues.\n- `expired_codes_free_capacity_before_the_caps_are_checked` — at the TTL boundary the sweep reclaims the account's slots and a new address is admitted.\n\nOracle: the caps are the invariant — map length never exceeds the bound and a refused issuance changes no existing entry.\n\nQueue: task 13829 (repo-health-code-pilot, lane code-x).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796776137&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7878&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7878&signature=86b36150509de52139df818ac5e28290bb4998ba0784fa8028d76b9f9718dee7\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7878?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T00:28:54Z","updated_at":"2026-11-15T13:16:25Z","closed_at":"2026-11-14T23:09:34Z","merged_at":"2026-11-14T23:09:33Z","merge_commit_sha":"3ff1d1e5d0c531896c9be084c5cf4d2a91aa9350","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":